      "created_at": "2026-10-14T14:30:01Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-14T14:30:01Z",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "GUI user gets nothing from psbt v2 today. GUI doesn't use the extensibility v2 provides and nothing in the GUI uses per-input locktimes. Meanwhile GUI users lose compatibility with pre-v32 nodes, possibly with external signers (I assume subset of hardware/software will fail to load/sign psbt v2), and disrupt any workflows where GUI-created PSBT is later passed to `joinpsbts` \"joinpsbts only operates on version 0 PSBTs (-8)\"\n\nWhy not simply have GUI-created PSBT default to v0 and get rid of this entire concern?",
